{"id":"9c3ae05f-5bde-4af3-b687-c38348334777","expr":"clazz == null || !clazz.getName().isEmpty()","rationale":"If clazz is non-null, its class name is expected to be a non-empty string as the proxy check relies on this.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#isCglibProxyClass(Class<?>):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:28.182445310Z"}
{"id":"90325750-e26c-42fc-a70f-83c08984b5dc","expr":"clazz == null || clazz.isInterface() == false","rationale":"The method most likely deals with concretes classes, so if clazz is not null, it is probably not an interface.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#isCglibProxyClass(Class<?>):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:28.182445310Z"}
{"id":"02ed4be5-fb67-4bca-9c98-8b0a5d78f63c","expr":"clazz == null || clazz.getName().contains(\"$\")","rationale":"If clazz is non-null, the class name is expected to contain the CGLIB separator character indicating proxy classes.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#isCglibProxyClass(Class<?>):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:28.182445310Z"}
{"id":"8f5f557e-8e0c-4c13-94af-9079d64f9e93","expr":"className != null || className == null","rationale":"To explicitly state nullness possibility.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#isCglibProxyClassName(String):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:28.201274471Z"}
{"id":"8f074da3-9be9-4923-b319-b3d67e607306","expr":"className == null || className.length() > 0","rationale":"Most class names are non-empty strings when non-null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#isCglibProxyClassName(String):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:28.201274471Z"}
{"id":"37dc8f6a-b3c2-4e24-9471-378f099db3d2","expr":"result == (className != null && className.contains(\"$$\"))","rationale":"The method returns true if and only if className is not null and contains the CGLIB class separator.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#isCglibProxyClassName(String):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:31.250056676Z"}
{"id":"9d279f69-8255-471b-9748-59a33d504f77","expr":"!result || (className != null && className.contains(\"$$\"))","rationale":"If the result is true, then className must be non-null and contain the separator.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#isCglibProxyClassName(String):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:31.250056676Z"}
{"id":"c965486a-9b6a-4bca-9e05-8df1c8719fcf","expr":"result == false || className != null","rationale":"The result can only be true if className is non-null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#isCglibProxyClassName(String):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:31.250056676Z"}
{"id":"2b10d43d-81e8-4261-9be5-92490a1446e5","expr":"className == null || !result","rationale":"If className is null, result must be false.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#isCglibProxyClassName(String):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:31.250056676Z"}
{"id":"edec645c-33eb-4f61-bef2-08890300e73b","expr":"result == className != null && className.indexOf(\"$$\") >= 0","rationale":"The result represents whether className is non-null and contains the CGLIB separator substring.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#isCglibProxyClassName(String):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:31.250056676Z"}
{"id":"cc442fbe-a4bf-42af-b9da-8f06f4c8a0f7","expr":"result == instance.getClass()","rationale":"The method returns getUserClass(instance.getClass()), and since this overrides getUserClass(Class<?>) which likely returns the original class, this invariant captures that the result matches the instance's runtime class in the typical case.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getUserClass(Object):Class<?>","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:31.702889073Z"}
