{"id":"c643867a-036f-4f9a-9cdb-80eee834dba9","expr":"result != null","rationale":"Since the method returns a package name string derived from clazz.getName() via getPackageName(String), the result should be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getPackageName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:51.871911525Z"}
{"id":"7c771e3f-aeb2-4b39-a469-09530abcfa9a","expr":"result.equals(\"\") || (result.indexOf('.') >= 0)","rationale":"The result is either an empty string (indicating default package) or contains at least one '.' as a package separator in the package name.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getPackageName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:51.871911525Z"}
{"id":"4049d9a2-02d3-42e6-9bfb-f83bea50f531","expr":"!result.contains(\"$\")","rationale":"The package name uses '.' not '$' as separator, so it should never contain '$'.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getPackageName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:51.871911525Z"}
{"id":"21547651-dce7-4b6e-a8bd-892e3ea4fa8f","expr":"result.equals(\"\") || result.equals(clazz.getPackageName())","rationale":"The method returns the package name consistent with the class's package name. The empty package should correspond to the default package.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getPackageName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:51.871911525Z"}
{"id":"f7e303b6-e50a-4310-b100-43610c1d34fd","expr":"result != null","rationale":"Method returns a string either substring or empty string, never null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getPackageName(String):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:53.863935206Z"}
{"id":"3960ae5d-f7b1-4b1b-ad17-21528a986d8b","expr":"(result.isEmpty() && !fqClassName.contains(\".\")) || (fqClassName.startsWith(result + \".\") || fqClassName.equals(result))","rationale":"If no dot separator, result is empty string; otherwise result is substring before last dot.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getPackageName(String):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:53.863935206Z"}
{"id":"5b347a2b-532a-4966-a10c-2ac6f194b66c","expr":"result.length() <= fqClassName.length()","rationale":"The resulting package name substring length is never larger than the original fqClassName string length.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getPackageName(String):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:53.863935206Z"}
{"id":"cbc450e5-0e2b-4d87-ae6b-498a7a61c47a","expr":"!result.isEmpty() || fqClassName.lastIndexOf('.') == -1","rationale":"Result is empty iff there is no dot in fqClassName.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getPackageName(String):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:53.863935206Z"}
{"id":"04b5e64d-570c-41fc-ba1e-aa0871edc7bb","expr":"clazz != null","rationale":"The method asserts that clazz must not be null, so this invariant holds at the method entry point.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getCanonicalName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:54.218768822Z"}
{"id":"6727bd4b-def4-4a2b-81e6-f7423e65b202","expr":"clazz.getCanonicalName() == null || clazz.getCanonicalName().equals(clazz.getTypeName()) || clazz.getCanonicalName().length() < clazz.getTypeName().length()","rationale":"The canonical name of the class may be null, in which case the typeName is used as fallback. Typically canonicalName is more canonical or simplified than typeName.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getCanonicalName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:54.218768822Z"}
{"id":"89b9183f-5ad7-4343-94f4-d27cf41bdded","expr":"!clazz.isPrimitive() || clazz.getCanonicalName().equals(clazz.getName())","rationale":"For primitive classes, the canonical name should match the name of the class.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getCanonicalName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:54.218768822Z"}
{"id":"192f282f-f4f8-4b52-a29e-a8a7d9bda6fa","expr":"clazz.getCanonicalName() == null || clazz.getCanonicalName().contains(\".\")","rationale":"Canonical names usually include package separators represented as dots.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getCanonicalName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:54.218768822Z"}
{"id":"a1142a16-8c8e-4bf1-a286-d17f762562de","expr":"clazz.getTypeName() != null && !clazz.getTypeName().isEmpty()","rationale":"The getTypeName() should always produce a non-null and non-empty string for any class.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getCanonicalName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:54.218768822Z"}
{"id":"3e74aade-dbd0-41d4-99b4-9beb90b49504","expr":"result != null","rationale":"The method never returns null; it either returns canonicalName or if null, clazz.getTypeName(), both non-null strings.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getCanonicalName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:54.757530445Z"}
{"id":"32b95cb4-fcc4-421b-9ad9-e0e733d1738c","expr":"result.equals(clazz.getCanonicalName()) || result.equals(clazz.getTypeName())","rationale":"The returned string is either the canonical name if it exists, otherwise the type name.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getCanonicalName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:54.757530445Z"}
{"id":"1869b6e5-3358-49d2-9423-4f12f8307ade","expr":"(clazz.getCanonicalName() != null) == result.equals(clazz.getCanonicalName())","rationale":"If the canonicalName is not null, the returned result should equal it; otherwise not.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getCanonicalName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:54.757530445Z"}
{"id":"1dfc3455-2b42-420d-b802-e2f8a1cf540a","expr":"(clazz.getCanonicalName() == null) == result.equals(clazz.getTypeName())","rationale":"If the canonicalName is null, the method returns typeName; otherwise it doesn't.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getCanonicalName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:54.757530445Z"}
{"id":"e9027c2e-451d-4c03-84eb-d8223916f95f","expr":"clazz != null","rationale":"Parameter clazz must not be null as asserted in the method.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:55.305934276Z"}
{"id":"e9bbabfd-4ece-4b12-b4c7-0a5548b47f68","expr":"clazz.getTypeName() != null","rationale":"clazz.getTypeName() returns a non-null string representing the class name.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:55.305934276Z"}
{"id":"b5c730c1-2929-4fe0-b90a-1dd76ab25169","expr":"clazz.isPrimitive() == false || clazz.getTypeName().equals(clazz.getName())","rationale":"For primitives, typeName equals the name; this captures a distinguishing relationship.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:55.305934276Z"}
{"id":"e6d2587c-9cb9-4247-ae67-6c3ae5f6ef48","expr":"clazz.getPackage() != null || clazz.getPackageName().isEmpty()","rationale":"Class either has a non-null package or is in the default package with an empty package name.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:55.305934276Z"}
{"id":"51f3696c-aca4-42ad-b685-1c1e168cacf0","expr":"!clazz.isArray() || clazz.getComponentType() != null","rationale":"If clazz is an array, getComponentType should return a non-null class.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:55.305934276Z"}
{"id":"a54f8743-75ea-47b8-b3be-8e06f6b52190","expr":"result.equals(clazz.getTypeName())","rationale":"The method always returns clazz.getTypeName(), so result must be equal to that.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:58.044696376Z"}
{"id":"9faee320-8b9a-4752-9762-b82a73f1e280","expr":"result != null","rationale":"Class.getTypeName() returns a non-null string, so result is non-null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:58.044696376Z"}
{"id":"6bd753ab-ec18-4c1c-8e33-f21316375ed5","expr":"result.length() > 0","rationale":"Class.getTypeName() returns strings representing class names which are non-empty.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:58.044696376Z"}
{"id":"6da95073-5e32-49e8-bad6-4e2bf42ba745","expr":"result.contains(\".\") || !result.contains(\"$\")","rationale":"Qualified names normally contain package names separated by dots; inner classes are indicated by '$'.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:58.044696376Z"}
{"id":"07e8fd1a-6b50-4f0a-9f41-0980bead5a05","expr":"method != null","rationale":"The method parameter is the input to getQualifiedMethodName and must be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedMethodName(Method):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:58.356047705Z"}
{"id":"d85d32ae-b793-4401-83f9-ad37b8ecfcee","expr":"method.getDeclaringClass() != null","rationale":"The declaring class of the method is required to build the qualified method name.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedMethodName(Method):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:58.356047705Z"}
{"id":"3393e049-545d-4033-b0d8-914c5c1aef62","expr":"method.getName() != null","rationale":"The method name is always non-null to identify the method.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedMethodName(Method):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:58.356047705Z"}
{"id":"b75d7a55-0d5d-4263-b158-7da120767e9e","expr":"method.getDeclaringClass().getName() != null","rationale":"The class name string must be non-null to build a qualified name.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedMethodName(Method):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:58.356047705Z"}
{"id":"66b24c88-2316-45c2-802e-8e6b2de04445","expr":"method.getDeclaringClass().isAssignableFrom(method.getDeclaringClass())","rationale":"This reflexive property is always true for the declaring class.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedMethodName(Method):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:58.356047705Z"}
{"id":"a894215b-79e4-4c5c-8f43-134a97e551c5","expr":"result != null","rationale":"The returned qualified method name string should not be null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedMethodName(Method):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:58.698131127Z"}
{"id":"6a950c51-62f7-46e0-a162-63d6162c6bfc","expr":"result.contains(method.getName())","rationale":"The result string includes the method's simple name.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedMethodName(Method):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:58.698131127Z"}
{"id":"31c491cf-31a4-4cac-8888-e6afac03df5b","expr":"result.startsWith(method.getDeclaringClass().getName())","rationale":"The result string includes the fully qualified declaring class name as prefix.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedMethodName(Method):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:58.698131127Z"}
{"id":"1011e080-0857-4dc1-a870-afc3bc874468","expr":"!result.isEmpty()","rationale":"The qualified method name result should not be empty.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedMethodName(Method):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:43:58.698131127Z"}
{"id":"b7894f01-fcdd-4a57-947a-0291641e89dc","expr":"method != null","rationale":"The method parameter must not be null as per method contract (asserted) and usage in method.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedMethodName(Method,Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:44:01.037999897Z"}
{"id":"9cb51046-11ea-4b3f-8c55-93a2fd14d2b2","expr":"clazz == null || clazz.isAssignableFrom(method.getDeclaringClass())","rationale":"If clazz is not null, then it is possible it is the same or a superclass/interface of method's declaring class.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedMethodName(Method,Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:44:01.037999897Z"}
{"id":"7582c0e7-d3db-4a7d-81f6-a5b93d5c5277","expr":"method.getDeclaringClass() != null","rationale":"Java reflection spec guarantees Method#getDeclaringClass() is non-null for valid methods.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedMethodName(Method,Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:44:01.037999897Z"}
{"id":"1a1f20fb-3e8b-43a8-934e-9f886b38793f","expr":"method.getName() != null && !method.getName().isEmpty()","rationale":"Method names are non-null and non-empty strings.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedMethodName(Method,Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:44:01.037999897Z"}
{"id":"260875c4-755a-4b5d-b412-98c1ea306e6d","expr":"(clazz == null || clazz.getName() != null) && method.getDeclaringClass().getName() != null","rationale":"Class#getName() never returns null; ensures safe usage of getName() in the method implementation.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedMethodName(Method,Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:44:01.037999897Z"}
{"id":"431d8c93-f121-4588-bf0d-1700b5a32754","expr":"clazz != null","rationale":"The clazz parameter should be valid and non-null as it's the target for constructor lookup.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#hasConstructor(Class<?>,Class<?>):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:44:02.872616541Z"}
{"id":"ddc2ad17-8701-4f78-9857-ad32a775a49e","expr":"paramTypes != null","rationale":"The paramTypes parameters array should be non-null to safely identify constructor signatures.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#hasConstructor(Class<?>,Class<?>):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:44:02.872616541Z"}
{"id":"82a57e58-ffe7-4aac-b184-2f2db79b4617","expr":"clazz.isAssignableFrom(clazz)","rationale":"Basic property that clazz is assignable from itself, reflecting valid class references used in the method.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#hasConstructor(Class<?>,Class<?>):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:44:02.872616541Z"}
{"id":"a8f0defe-12de-4c59-9906-119abc229685","expr":"paramTypes.getClass().isArray()","rationale":"paramTypes is expected to be a varargs array of Class<?> representing constructor parameters.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#hasConstructor(Class<?>,Class<?>):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:44:02.872616541Z"}
{"id":"4e4d2558-44e2-4f51-8c72-296c7b390eed","expr":"result != null","rationale":"The result string is composed of non-null class name and method name, so it must be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedMethodName(Method,Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:44:02.916325725Z"}
{"id":"5b91e57b-7aa5-437e-a977-093d1dd02811","expr":"(clazz != null && result.startsWith(clazz.getName() + \".\")) || (clazz == null && result.startsWith(method.getDeclaringClass().getName() + \".\"))","rationale":"If clazz is non-null, result starts with clazz name plus dot; otherwise, it starts with the declaring class name plus dot.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedMethodName(Method,Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:44:02.916325725Z"}
{"id":"83f4c0bb-8adb-44aa-ae07-f7fde6181342","expr":"result.endsWith(method.getName())","rationale":"Result is qualified method name in the form of 'className.methodName', so it must end with the method's name.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedMethodName(Method,Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:44:02.916325725Z"}
{"id":"bd34c00e-7de2-4bd6-a4ea-0807aa205699","expr":"result.equals((clazz != null ? clazz : method.getDeclaringClass()).getName() + \".\" + method.getName())","rationale":"The method returns precisely the concatenation of the chosen class name, a dot, and the method's name.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedMethodName(Method,Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:44:02.916325725Z"}
{"id":"8a52d769-09e2-4ece-8074-411359b403a8","expr":"paramTypes != null","rationale":"paramTypes must be a non-null array valid for the getConstructor call.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getConstructorIfAvailable(Class<T>,Class<?>):Constructor<T>","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:44:05.408615994Z"}
{"id":"67f70b45-5559-4cd6-950b-89f9442593f2","expr":"clazz.isInterface() == false","rationale":"Typically clazz is not an interface because getConstructor won't find constructors for interfaces.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getConstructorIfAvailable(Class<T>,Class<?>):Constructor<T>","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:44:05.408615994Z"}
{"id":"3143fcd9-e0e4-4b80-b12e-e172721b7ba8","expr":"clazz != null","rationale":"The method asserts that clazz must not be null before proceeding.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#hasMethod(Class<?>,Method):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:44:07.011501146Z"}
{"id":"d3dc154e-34cb-4f36-9688-2a72633ee4da","expr":"method != null","rationale":"The method asserts that method must not be null before proceeding.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#hasMethod(Class<?>,Method):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:44:07.011501146Z"}
{"id":"ac01bcaf-ac34-44ee-9b0a-77d758670536","expr":"method.getDeclaringClass() != null","rationale":"Given method is non-null, its declaring class is expected to be non-null as per Method contract.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#hasMethod(Class<?>,Method):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:44:07.011501146Z"}
{"id":"39ae7c59-a131-4bef-8f60-e63944eb499f","expr":"method.getName() != null && !method.getName().isEmpty()","rationale":"Method names are typically non-null and not empty, which is implied by the Method contract.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#hasMethod(Class<?>,Method):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:44:07.011501146Z"}
{"id":"9a31334f-9b24-4fa0-ab68-8f31f57e095b","expr":"(clazz == method.getDeclaringClass()) || (clazz != method.getDeclaringClass())","rationale":"This logical tautology helps understand the two main branches of the method logic.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#hasMethod(Class<?>,Method):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:44:07.011501146Z"}
{"id":"4c8a7f97-1969-44e2-9421-64b04868f37a","expr":"result == null || result.getModifiers() == result.getModifiers()","rationale":"A trivial invariant to emphasize that result's modifiers are stable; can be considered for further extension.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getConstructorIfAvailable(Class<T>,Class<?>):Constructor<T>","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:44:08.171959335Z"}
{"id":"5f93f84f-ebde-4031-bf93-73bdfbcf51c2","expr":"result == null || result.getParameterTypes().length == paramTypes.length","rationale":"Ensures the found constructor's parameter count matches requested paramTypes length.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getConstructorIfAvailable(Class<T>,Class<?>):Constructor<T>","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:44:08.171959335Z"}
{"id":"550fc253-d40c-4872-94e8-e81b9205cbca","expr":"! (result != null && paramTypes == null)","rationale":"Protects against null paramTypes when a constructor is returned.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getConstructorIfAvailable(Class<T>,Class<?>):Constructor<T>","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:44:08.171959335Z"}
{"id":"8cab8fd9-d839-410d-9eb1-17b91caa569f","expr":"clazz != null","rationale":"The method checks for methods on the class, so clazz must not be null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#hasMethod(Class<?>,String,Class<?>):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:44:09.335055105Z"}
{"id":"8ea1fdd3-b49d-487d-956c-3f77b415ccbb","expr":"methodName != null","rationale":"Method names must be valid strings for lookup.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#hasMethod(Class<?>,String,Class<?>):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:44:09.335055105Z"}
