{"id":"e98c41e8-51b4-419f-83f6-58b54409105a","expr":"o == null || o.getClass() != null","rationale":"If o is not null, calling getClass() will not throw, so this is always true unless o is null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.core.style.DefaultToStringStyler#styleEnd(StringBuilder,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/core/style/DefaultToStringStyler.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:49:08.795684678Z"}
{"id":"54c3f8b6-0ef4-460a-93b9-bd6dc726f7db","expr":"o == null || o.toString() != null","rationale":"Typically toString returns a non-null string, useful for further styling in other methods.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.core.style.DefaultToStringStyler#styleEnd(StringBuilder,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/core/style/DefaultToStringStyler.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:49:08.795684678Z"}
