{"id":"354baccd-9dab-4221-938f-7521b1ed7ed7","expr":"className != null","rationale":"The method calls className.split, which would throw NullPointerException if className were null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.aot.hint.SimpleTypeReference#isValidClassName(String):boolean","file":"org/springframework/aot/hint/SimpleTypeReference.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:16:10.338828099Z"}
{"id":"e40d5787-be5b-42a2-a690-bea9cbaae6ac","expr":"className.length() > 0","rationale":"A valid class name is expected to have at least one character.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.aot.hint.SimpleTypeReference#isValidClassName(String):boolean","file":"org/springframework/aot/hint/SimpleTypeReference.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:16:10.338828099Z"}
{"id":"324fccf3-cc74-44fd-88ae-bc520d29a353","expr":"!className.endsWith(\".\")","rationale":"Because className.split uses \\., -1, trailing empty segments are preserved, which would fail the identifier check.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.aot.hint.SimpleTypeReference#isValidClassName(String):boolean","file":"org/springframework/aot/hint/SimpleTypeReference.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:16:10.338828099Z"}
{"id":"55abe5c7-7b2b-49c1-b7e0-b974ae7b14a3","expr":"!className.startsWith(\".\")","rationale":"Leading dot would cause the first segment after split to be empty, which is not a valid identifier.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.aot.hint.SimpleTypeReference#isValidClassName(String):boolean","file":"org/springframework/aot/hint/SimpleTypeReference.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:16:10.338828099Z"}
{"id":"367df7dc-d796-46aa-b79a-3e072406d5b7","expr":"className.indexOf('[') == -1 || className.indexOf(']') != -1","rationale":"The method removes '[' and ']' before checking identifiers, so if '[' exists, ']' should also exist to avoid malformed segments.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.aot.hint.SimpleTypeReference#isValidClassName(String):boolean","file":"org/springframework/aot/hint/SimpleTypeReference.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:16:10.338828099Z"}
{"id":"fbca6b61-9f18-40a3-9f02-3a8858fc1e74","expr":"className != null && !className.isEmpty()","rationale":"The input string must be non-null and typically non-empty for meaningful processing.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.aot.hint.SimpleTypeReference#createTypeReference(String):SimpleTypeReference","file":"org/springframework/aot/hint/SimpleTypeReference.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:16:10.638924671Z"}
{"id":"17f4378d-7f71-45ef-bcbd-217e8dd4e65a","expr":"className.lastIndexOf('.') >= -1","rationale":"lastIndexOf returns -1 if the character is not found, so it's always >= -1.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.aot.hint.SimpleTypeReference#createTypeReference(String):SimpleTypeReference","file":"org/springframework/aot/hint/SimpleTypeReference.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:16:10.638924671Z"}
{"id":"c253df9f-fb90-4cc8-9b8c-6959efd5e106","expr":"(className.lastIndexOf('.') != -1) || (className.lastIndexOf('.') == -1)","rationale":"branch condition depends on the value of lastIndexOf('.').","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.aot.hint.SimpleTypeReference#createTypeReference(String):SimpleTypeReference","file":"org/springframework/aot/hint/SimpleTypeReference.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:16:10.638924671Z"}
{"id":"dcd09a8f-5e8a-4a3b-a5a1-e54551d85e51","expr":"(className.lastIndexOf('.') != -1) == false || className.substring(0, className.lastIndexOf('.')).length() >= 0","rationale":"If lastIndexOf('.') != -1, then 0 <= lastIndexOf('.') so substring arguments are correct.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.aot.hint.SimpleTypeReference#createTypeReference(String):SimpleTypeReference","file":"org/springframework/aot/hint/SimpleTypeReference.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:16:10.638924671Z"}
{"id":"1dbf99da-1bac-4b1d-b7ad-a0ce52d9b2b8","expr":"!result || className.length() > 0","rationale":"If the className is valid, it cannot be empty, else the single segment would be empty and thus invalid.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.aot.hint.SimpleTypeReference#isValidClassName(String):boolean","file":"org/springframework/aot/hint/SimpleTypeReference.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:16:10.884553103Z"}
{"id":"fe13cfb8-a114-4f9b-9eb4-2d9c6a1d1c82","expr":"!result || !className.contains(\" \")","rationale":"If the className is valid, none of its segments contain spaces, since identifiers cannot have spaces.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.aot.hint.SimpleTypeReference#isValidClassName(String):boolean","file":"org/springframework/aot/hint/SimpleTypeReference.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:16:10.884553103Z"}
{"id":"031e9330-9b1b-4a12-becb-236edb487f8e","expr":"!result || !className.startsWith(\".\") && !className.endsWith(\".\")","rationale":"If the result is true, then the className does not have empty segments at ends caused by leading or trailing dots.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.aot.hint.SimpleTypeReference#isValidClassName(String):boolean","file":"org/springframework/aot/hint/SimpleTypeReference.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:16:10.884553103Z"}
{"id":"c73e0f27-a875-4589-b6f2-27e9a0504827","expr":"result != null","rationale":"The method always constructs and returns a new SimpleTypeReference object.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.aot.hint.SimpleTypeReference#createTypeReference(String):SimpleTypeReference","file":"org/springframework/aot/hint/SimpleTypeReference.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:16:12.156486795Z"}
{"id":"cf3aa235-d66c-4fe5-9aa1-080e0c2b367c","expr":"result.getCanonicalName().equals(className)","rationale":"createTypeReference builds the SimpleTypeReference from className, preserving the canonical name.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.aot.hint.SimpleTypeReference#createTypeReference(String):SimpleTypeReference","file":"org/springframework/aot/hint/SimpleTypeReference.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:16:12.156486795Z"}
{"id":"d30d24bd-4806-430a-9163-536568acf6f5","expr":"(className.lastIndexOf('.') != -1) == (result.getCanonicalName().contains(\".\"))","rationale":"If className contains '.', the package and type names are split, so canonicalName includes '.'; otherwise, it may not.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.aot.hint.SimpleTypeReference#createTypeReference(String):SimpleTypeReference","file":"org/springframework/aot/hint/SimpleTypeReference.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:16:12.156486795Z"}
{"id":"d93cdda4-806e-4c47-9ab5-40c9b7b3b757","expr":"className.lastIndexOf('.') == -1 || result.getCanonicalName().startsWith(className.substring(0, className.lastIndexOf('.')) + \".\")","rationale":"When className contains a package, result's canonical name must start with the package name followed by a dot.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.aot.hint.SimpleTypeReference#createTypeReference(String):SimpleTypeReference","file":"org/springframework/aot/hint/SimpleTypeReference.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:16:12.156486795Z"}
{"id":"6914ef2b-adae-4877-bdc7-57d9d19802f8","expr":"result.getCanonicalName().endsWith(className.substring(className.lastIndexOf('.') + 1))","rationale":"The canonicalName must end with the simple class name from the input className.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.aot.hint.SimpleTypeReference#createTypeReference(String):SimpleTypeReference","file":"org/springframework/aot/hint/SimpleTypeReference.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:16:12.156486795Z"}
