{"id":"0a4a6112-21d5-4303-9e67-64ae43e0bae3","expr":"result != null && !result.isEmpty()","rationale":"The method returns a canonical name which should always be a valid fully qualified name string, never null or empty.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.aot.hint.SimpleTypeReference#getCanonicalName():String","file":"org/springframework/aot/hint/SimpleTypeReference.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:16:13.720625691Z"}
{"id":"7bf937ee-dcde-4411-8722-2e35b0d44767","expr":"!result.contains(\" \")","rationale":"Canonical type names typically do not have spaces as they represent fully qualified Java type names.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.aot.hint.SimpleTypeReference#getCanonicalName():String","file":"org/springframework/aot/hint/SimpleTypeReference.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:16:13.720625691Z"}
{"id":"067b933f-49d8-4a18-8c8d-2d243851bba9","expr":"result.indexOf('.') >= 0 || (result.length() > 0 && Character.isJavaIdentifierStart(result.charAt(0)))","rationale":"A canonical name either includes package qualifiers separated by '.' or is a simple type name starting with a valid identifier character.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.aot.hint.SimpleTypeReference#getCanonicalName():String","file":"org/springframework/aot/hint/SimpleTypeReference.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:16:13.720625691Z"}
{"id":"41157fea-0744-46af-929a-529213ac4af8","expr":"result.length() == 0 || Character.isJavaIdentifierPart(result.charAt(result.length() - 1))","rationale":"Java canonical names end with a valid identifier part character; this ensures the last character is valid if result is not empty.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.aot.hint.SimpleTypeReference#getCanonicalName():String","file":"org/springframework/aot/hint/SimpleTypeReference.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:16:13.720625691Z"}
