{"id":"d1df9ad7-f9c5-4f60-bc77-f1c354ec2e76","expr":"name != null","rationale":"Typically, the 'name' parameter for a class visitor is non-null because it represents the internal name of the class.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.AbstractClassFilterTransformer#visit(int,int,String,String,String,String[]):void","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/AbstractClassFilterTransformer.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:21:56.156945173Z"}
{"id":"0709fec3-9dd3-423c-8455-c28a2b7f2b91","expr":"superName != null || (access & 0x200) != 0","rationale":"In Java bytecode, an interface has ACC_INTERFACE set (0x200). Interfaces do not have superclasses, so superName might be null only if the class is an interface.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.AbstractClassFilterTransformer#visit(int,int,String,String,String,String[]):void","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/AbstractClassFilterTransformer.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:21:56.156945173Z"}
