{"id":"41f1b4bb-e938-4d3a-8a26-ddb3193b41c8","expr":"numLocal >= 0","rationale":"The number of local variables (numLocal) represents a count and thus is non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFrame(int,int,Object[],int,Object[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:43.067628713Z"}
{"id":"2bfcebaa-7eab-4695-8a37-c3a786945cab","expr":"numStack >= 0","rationale":"The number of stack elements (numStack) also represents a count and must be non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFrame(int,int,Object[],int,Object[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:43.067628713Z"}
{"id":"5d17c1dd-98cf-47eb-8438-62a722bec647","expr":"(local == null || local.length >= numLocal)","rationale":"If local array is not null, its length must be at least equal to numLocal.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFrame(int,int,Object[],int,Object[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:43.067628713Z"}
{"id":"52fcb786-ff49-4f5e-93e8-d9d9b488513b","expr":"(stack == null || stack.length >= numStack)","rationale":"If stack array is not null, its length must be at least equal to numStack.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFrame(int,int,Object[],int,Object[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:43.067628713Z"}
{"id":"cf0d26b0-4a05-47f3-9d34-b16915348a24","expr":"type == 0 || type == 1 || type == 2 || type == 3 || type == 4 || type == 5","rationale":"The 'type' parameter represents specific frame types and thus must be one of predefined constants.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFrame(int,int,Object[],int,Object[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:43.067628713Z"}
{"id":"200cdf1c-8fc4-4b7d-bfb2-d569a10181f0","expr":"type >= 0 && type <= 8","rationale":"type is one of the ASM frame type constants indicating frame kind.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFrame(int,int,Object[],int,Object[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:43.663141860Z"}
{"id":"7ccc5e7e-4f5c-4bc7-8379-57a6517b706f","expr":"numLocal >= 0 && (local == null || local.length >= numLocal)","rationale":"Ensures local array length consistency with numLocal.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFrame(int,int,Object[],int,Object[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:43.663141860Z"}
{"id":"fb5111b7-ab37-4df8-b8c1-4612fc9550bb","expr":"numStack >= 0 && (stack == null || stack.length >= numStack)","rationale":"Ensures stack array length consistency with numStack.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFrame(int,int,Object[],int,Object[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:43.663141860Z"}
{"id":"a2a3f372-015a-4f3e-b9b1-37cf86e8dea9","expr":"(type != 0) || (numLocal >= 0 && numStack >= 0)","rationale":"Natural requirement for new frames.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFrame(int,int,Object[],int,Object[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:43.663141860Z"}
{"id":"55e0a072-bb27-4aa5-91c4-e0b2a4addb53","expr":"(numStack == 0) || (stack != null && stack.length >= numStack)","rationale":"Correctness of stack array sizing relative to numStack.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFrame(int,int,Object[],int,Object[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:43.663141860Z"}
{"id":"4930686e-1c48-4bdb-8f47-c8f42b3f5e2d","expr":"opcode >= 0","rationale":"Opcode values for JVM instructions are non-negative integers as per JVM specification.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInsn(int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:44.441130856Z"}
{"id":"c4411f2f-b088-4b74-b04a-2c630084b17a","expr":"opcode >= 0","rationale":"The opcode parameter is an opcode of a JVM instruction, which are typically non-negative integer constants.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInsn(int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:44.796119402Z"}
{"id":"d2013ec1-f4c4-4894-b110-086b9d76561e","expr":"opcode >= 0 && opcode < 256","rationale":"In JVM, opcodes are byte-sized and thus valid opcodes fall within 0 to 255.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInsn(int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:44.796119402Z"}
{"id":"a0ed40b2-2cb7-49d9-b841-7aab66c2771c","expr":"operand >= 0","rationale":"Operand is non-negative, as negative operands are not expected for these opcodes.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitIntInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:44.951171099Z"}
{"id":"8a561874-c03c-4b46-8e48-7586cd81a191","expr":"owner != null","rationale":"The JVM requires an owner class name for field instructions.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFieldInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:47.272191647Z"}
{"id":"095c2b25-876d-43c4-b3ef-5adf9547efc2","expr":"name != null","rationale":"The field name must be non-null to identify the field being accessed.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFieldInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:47.272191647Z"}
{"id":"2067fa80-1cde-441e-aca1-399399fad160","expr":"descriptor != null","rationale":"The field descriptor (type) must be non-null to describe the field type.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFieldInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:47.272191647Z"}
{"id":"f03e3f90-0a90-42ef-8b32-a47fd32f751c","expr":"(opcode >= 178 && opcode <= 181)","rationale":"The opcode must be one of GETSTATIC(178), PUTSTATIC(179), GETFIELD(180), PUTFIELD(181).","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFieldInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:47.272191647Z"}
{"id":"87f3a06b-1203-4919-808c-42dde67e60ed","expr":"(descriptor.length() > 0)","rationale":"The descriptor string should be a non-empty valid type descriptor.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFieldInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:47.272191647Z"}
{"id":"81c5d9e6-3330-490e-afd5-d9bdb579f797","expr":"(opcode >= 21 && opcode <= 54) || opcode == 169","rationale":"The method processes var instructions identified by JVM opcodes related to variable load/store and RET.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:48.183848303Z"}
{"id":"1ed7c772-fe97-4d42-8ca8-7fc157ed7f8b","expr":"varIndex >= 0","rationale":"Local variable indices in JVM bytecode are non-negative integers.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:48.183848303Z"}
{"id":"8f76cff5-2cac-47e8-8d08-7552c0b623a7","expr":"(varIndex < 4) == (opcode != 169)","rationale":"The path for optimized opcode applies only when varIndex < 4 and opcode is not RET.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:48.183848303Z"}
{"id":"bc88148e-c110-4994-91d9-19993d90db37","expr":"varIndex < 256 || (varIndex >= 256 && varIndex < 65536)","rationale":"The method treats differently varIndex values above or below 256, corresponding to JVM instruction encoding requirements.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:48.183848303Z"}
{"id":"6faeeeaf-c5ce-438e-bc4f-3d8e6c850154","expr":"opcode != 0","rationale":"visitVarInsn is expected to receive a valid variable instruction opcode.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:48.183848303Z"}
{"id":"a4137c3c-8332-49a6-ba7a-6225c456523a","expr":"varIndex >= 0","rationale":"varIndex as a variable index in bytecode must be non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:48.797642485Z"}
{"id":"8f93f41c-51cd-4f98-84af-08b7eed52903","expr":"varIndex < 256 || varIndex >= 256","rationale":"Code branches depending on whether varIndex is less than 256 or not.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:48.797642485Z"}
{"id":"e8a3b2fe-d3c9-4259-93db-c70de2ed085a","expr":"opcode >= 0","rationale":"Opcode must be a valid JVM opcode integer (non-negative).","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:48.797642485Z"}
{"id":"098d1f7d-10cf-4745-85a1-992bebd7a87b","expr":"type != null","rationale":"The parameter 'type' is expected to be a valid internal name of a class, so it cannot be null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTypeInsn(int,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:49.607006317Z"}
{"id":"44cabf52-c764-407e-9685-0cb3e94cb4a6","expr":"type.length() > 0","rationale":"As the type string represents a class descriptor internal name, it must be nonempty.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTypeInsn(int,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:49.607006317Z"}
{"id":"51108d47-ec00-4680-b456-9fdb5c4c89e5","expr":"opcode >= 0","rationale":"Opcodes used must be non-negative integer values.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTypeInsn(int,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:49.607006317Z"}
{"id":"85a0b9e3-ca2c-4c02-9055-d287fe58e9dd","expr":"type != null","rationale":"The type parameter represents a non-null internal name of a class or interface, used for constant class addition.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTypeInsn(int,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:50.437937614Z"}
{"id":"4b9b06d3-37b0-454f-be2a-98cfd78d2cee","expr":"opcode >= 0","rationale":"opcode is an integer representing a JVM bytecode instruction opcode, which should be non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTypeInsn(int,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:50.437937614Z"}
{"id":"519c5716-4d15-45c1-ab81-88efde64124e","expr":"opcode == 187 || opcode == 189 || opcode == 192 || opcode == 193","rationale":"The method handles type instructions which typically include NEW(187), ANEWARRAY(189), CHECKCAST(192), INSTANCEOF(193).","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTypeInsn(int,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:50.437937614Z"}
{"id":"1b94781e-2ea4-4a5a-913a-289730e1fef7","expr":"type.length() > 0","rationale":"The type string should be a valid internal name, thus non-empty.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTypeInsn(int,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:50.437937614Z"}
{"id":"3930f0d1-0c54-47c9-8513-dcc03b6867fe","expr":"!type.contains(\" \")","rationale":"The type internal name does not contain whitespace.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTypeInsn(int,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:50.437937614Z"}
{"id":"70702950-20fb-43e2-8dbc-678d5afd7f52","expr":"owner != null","rationale":"The 'owner' parameter represents the internal name of the class where the method is declared, so it should not be null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMethodInsn(int,String,String,String,boolean):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:51.493642389Z"}
{"id":"abe43b88-731e-40e4-8fb1-2098b9de4d9f","expr":"name != null","rationale":"The 'name' parameter is the name of the method to be invoked and should not be null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMethodInsn(int,String,String,String,boolean):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:51.493642389Z"}
{"id":"3e839712-12d8-4ef2-817f-d552fafe7abb","expr":"descriptor != null","rationale":"The 'descriptor' parameter describes the signature of the method and should not be null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMethodInsn(int,String,String,String,boolean):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:51.493642389Z"}
{"id":"365856dd-2b86-4ec7-8708-e5c5c1769ffe","expr":"owner != null && name != null && descriptor != null","rationale":"These strings represent the field owner, name, and descriptor, which must be non-null for the field reference addition to work correctly.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFieldInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:51.942997506Z"}
{"id":"e5039c10-d021-4623-a9d8-6396bbc5ea11","expr":"descriptor.length() > 0","rationale":"We read descriptor.charAt(0) thus descriptor.length() must be positive.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFieldInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:51.942997506Z"}
{"id":"82942952-d2d8-4ce0-a9fe-c00a99836814","expr":"name.length() > 0","rationale":"Field name string length is expected to be positive to identify the field.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFieldInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:51.942997506Z"}
{"id":"d737d4d0-dc72-4a3e-8c8c-53b27df3a6ff","expr":"owner != null && name != null && descriptor != null","rationale":"owner, name and descriptor are used to create the methodrefSymbol, so they must be non-null here.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMethodInsn(int,String,String,String,boolean):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:52.022468770Z"}
{"id":"679c9b3f-4434-4aaa-9730-61a4d175d647","expr":"descriptor.startsWith(\"(\") && descriptor.contains(\")\")","rationale":"The descriptor string represents the method signature, which should include parameters and return type formatted with parentheses.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMethodInsn(int,String,String,String,boolean):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:52.022468770Z"}
{"id":"c95183ef-b1a5-4dcd-973c-3e76ee4d027b","expr":"name != null","rationale":"The method name should not be null because it's used as a key for constant pool entries.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInvokeDynamicInsn(String,String,Handle,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:52.827084004Z"}
{"id":"3b8c250d-7b1f-4cc3-97d9-ca423946e758","expr":"descriptor != null","rationale":"The method descriptor (signature) must be non-null to describe the method arguments and return types.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInvokeDynamicInsn(String,String,Handle,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:52.827084004Z"}
{"id":"25252575-c4f1-4798-9248-11dad35729d0","expr":"bootstrapMethodHandle != null","rationale":"Bootstrap method handle is required for invokedynamic instructions.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInvokeDynamicInsn(String,String,Handle,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:52.827084004Z"}
{"id":"13736a14-832a-414e-9f22-518a5984c744","expr":"bootstrapMethodArguments == null || bootstrapMethodArguments.getClass().isArray()","rationale":"The bootstrapMethodArguments parameter is a varargs array (Object[]).","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInvokeDynamicInsn(String,String,Handle,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:52.827084004Z"}
{"id":"c7256b67-e1b0-4580-a403-3e4115cad7df","expr":"name.length() > 0","rationale":"Method name should be non-empty string.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInvokeDynamicInsn(String,String,Handle,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:52.827084004Z"}
{"id":"c5e34a54-4b2b-4db6-87ae-2f829d64a80e","expr":"name != null","rationale":"The 'name' parameter must be non-null to specify the method name for the invokedynamic instruction.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInvokeDynamicInsn(String,String,Handle,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:53.560525427Z"}
{"id":"97096597-f786-4dd2-bd5a-ff389f76b58a","expr":"descriptor != null","rationale":"The 'descriptor' parameter must be non-null as it represents the method descriptor.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInvokeDynamicInsn(String,String,Handle,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:53.560525427Z"}
{"id":"373f6221-6a34-40b0-9d97-741fbbeb9ef6","expr":"bootstrapMethodHandle != null","rationale":"The 'bootstrapMethodHandle' parameter must be non-null as it identifies the bootstrap method.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInvokeDynamicInsn(String,String,Handle,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:53.560525427Z"}
{"id":"8d9a9c03-6811-44c1-b00e-53b668839f59","expr":"bootstrapMethodArguments != null","rationale":"The 'bootstrapMethodArguments' array is non-null to hold any bootstrap method arguments.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInvokeDynamicInsn(String,String,Handle,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:53.560525427Z"}
{"id":"18734c1b-9dc9-4fa6-b9f8-4792cbf3b011","expr":"name.length() > 0","rationale":"The 'name' parameter should be a non-empty string representing the method name.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInvokeDynamicInsn(String,String,Handle,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:53.560525427Z"}
{"id":"7987aa0c-9203-430b-adac-5cbf0677cc67","expr":"label != null","rationale":"label is used with field accesses and methods, so it must be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitJumpInsn(int,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:54.531332864Z"}
{"id":"835f7e1f-eedf-4a8d-a4d5-7dce882e247b","expr":"opcode >= 0","rationale":"opcode represents a JVM opcode which are non-negative integers.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitJumpInsn(int,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:54.531332864Z"}
{"id":"c2501f9f-5d10-4e3c-a5de-4e4e6791483e","expr":"label != null","rationale":"The label parameter is used to specify the jump target and must be a valid non-null object.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitJumpInsn(int,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:54.694866561Z"}
{"id":"00e3d1a9-6366-472b-8be2-72622a467c9b","expr":"opcode >= 0","rationale":"Bytecode opcodes are non-negative integers representing instructions.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitJumpInsn(int,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:54.694866561Z"}
{"id":"282d3f3f-0e17-4b60-98f6-15898a024885","expr":"label.getCanonicalInstance() == label","rationale":"Ensures the label is canonical at this point before modification as the method uses label.getCanonicalInstance() to set jump flags.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitJumpInsn(int,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:54.694866561Z"}
{"id":"b04882f3-3640-4d00-ab35-dd3d0cd74371","expr":"value != null","rationale":"The value parameter is generally expected to be a constant object for the LDC instruction and usually isn't null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLdcInsn(Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:55.523580525Z"}
{"id":"19381039-f13d-43cc-91f2-5eadf658820c","expr":"label != null","rationale":"The method uses label's fields and methods assuming it's non-null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLabel(Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:55.533063183Z"}
{"id":"3aa15a66-f0f5-45eb-a88f-2c3b087a9bcb","expr":"label != null","rationale":"The label parameter should be non-null as it's used to identify code positions.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLabel(Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:55.700140385Z"}
{"id":"8c2f54fb-0886-4c92-9cef-b5a5400b44bc","expr":"label.bytecodeOffset >= 0","rationale":"Labels represent positions in code, so the bytecode offset should be non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLabel(Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:55.700140385Z"}
{"id":"91055865-18dc-4c9b-a219-15a7502e70e5","expr":"label.frame == null || label.frame.owner == label","rationale":"The frame, if set, should be either null or owned by the label.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLabel(Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:55.700140385Z"}
{"id":"bc8a7699-e671-41bc-bba2-7bd0ca7c32e5","expr":"label.nextBasicBlock == null || label.nextBasicBlock.bytecodeOffset > label.bytecodeOffset","rationale":"The list of basic blocks should be ordered by bytecode offset ascending.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLabel(Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:55.700140385Z"}
{"id":"de02f9fc-5fa1-4aae-9adf-2c26b00dd917","expr":"varIndex >= 0","rationale":"Local variable indices are non-negative integers.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:57.369597674Z"}
{"id":"81c2e16e-df51-4023-bab6-5bf789bebc43","expr":"increment >= -32768 && increment <= 32767","rationale":"Increment is stored as a short in wide mode; its full int value fits in a short range.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:57.369597674Z"}
{"id":"bb545380-a514-4e38-9bf2-650e929ae1e5","expr":"(varIndex > 255) || (increment > 127) || (increment < -128) || (!(varIndex > 255) && !(increment > 127) && !(increment < -128))","rationale":"The control flow uses varIndex and increment values to choose wide or normal IINC instruction.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:57.369597674Z"}
{"id":"350049d8-f659-4966-a5ba-8b50c909187d","expr":"increment <= 127 || increment >= -128","rationale":"The non-wide opcode expects increment in byte range (-128 to 127).","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:57.369597674Z"}
{"id":"3faedb46-926d-4153-b55a-e1ebf40d253f","expr":"labels != null","rationale":"The labels parameter is a varargs array and must be non-null for the method to work correctly.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:58.029324683Z"}
{"id":"34033676-b9c0-4e39-8cb7-bfcd06df231a","expr":"labels.length >= (max - min + 1)","rationale":"The labels array should have at least one label per case in the range between min and max.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:58.029324683Z"}
{"id":"9b5cb9e9-62a6-4c55-af12-e606d642d9d5","expr":"min <= max","rationale":"The min parameter should be less than or equal to max to define a valid switch range.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:58.029324683Z"}
{"id":"74b4d8bd-968e-4056-947d-5c02af1d6463","expr":"dflt != null","rationale":"The default label must not be null because it is used as a fallback target for the switch.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:58.029324683Z"}
{"id":"cfb0b241-7365-4357-b4ae-8999d9fa287e","expr":"dflt != null","rationale":"Default label for lookup switch instructions must be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:58.739023409Z"}
{"id":"f930dd37-d956-45ef-898e-af00271b351c","expr":"keys != null","rationale":"Keys array for lookup switch instructions must be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:58.739023409Z"}
{"id":"a7368383-ef7c-4e52-a2c7-a016ef0907ee","expr":"labels != null","rationale":"Labels array must be non-null for the lookup switch.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:58.739023409Z"}
{"id":"7a04231b-feb1-4d2c-9023-75ff6b7a32a3","expr":"labels.length == keys.length","rationale":"Each key corresponds to exactly one label in lookup switch.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:58.739023409Z"}
{"id":"d24563c3-32e6-44dd-ba4a-00af7b532f8a","expr":"labels.length >= 0","rationale":"Lengths of keys and labels arrays cannot be negative.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:58.739023409Z"}
{"id":"94402953-fc51-44ac-988b-d2a0c93a549b","expr":"(varIndex >= 0)","rationale":"In JVM bytecode, variable index must be non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:58.928779221Z"}
{"id":"58bbeb01-0c5e-469a-a787-3425132eb230","expr":"increment >= -128 && increment <= 127","rationale":"The increment value is a signed 8-bit integer or else the instruction is emitted WIDE.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:58.928779221Z"}
{"id":"2d05c62a-9bcc-4758-a557-263f622bc451","expr":"labels != null","rationale":"The method iterates over labels, so labels must be non-null at method exit.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:59.106858507Z"}
{"id":"a1b3e5cb-1c2d-4285-9a67-40c371a86c1a","expr":"max >= min","rationale":"For a table switch instruction, the max key value must be >= min to define a valid range.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:59.106858507Z"}
{"id":"b0c21777-d0bd-4c84-8b7d-8562bca24b5a","expr":"labels.length == max - min + 1","rationale":"labels array length corresponds to the entries in the table switch between min and max keys.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:59.106858507Z"}
{"id":"e9ce6086-c48d-444d-a20f-df14371e42a1","expr":"dflt != null","rationale":"dflt label must be valid as it is put in the bytecode unconditionally.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:28:59.106858507Z"}
{"id":"46e3fb41-5ca3-4661-8a0c-48fdbb65808a","expr":"keys != null && labels != null","rationale":"The method processes keys and labels arrays, so neither should be null at this point.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:29:00.385828678Z"}
{"id":"860f86db-5871-40de-b8ff-76688ea683f4","expr":"keys.length == labels.length","rationale":"The keys and labels arrays should be of equal length because each key corresponds to a label.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:29:00.385828678Z"}
{"id":"5f017758-e183-40b5-adef-e5aa681bf048","expr":"dflt != null","rationale":"The default label is used and must always be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:29:00.385828678Z"}
{"id":"09c90774-6139-4e76-a5cd-3bb430be6d2a","expr":"labels.length >= 0","rationale":"Array length is guaranteed to be non-negative in Java.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:29:00.385828678Z"}
{"id":"0a8772f1-7d9b-4872-9256-c292671c0cc0","expr":"keys.length >= 0","rationale":"Array length is guaranteed to be non-negative in Java.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:29:00.385828678Z"}
{"id":"c15c7bcf-30af-435d-8adf-2a703605195d","expr":"dflt != null","rationale":"The default label for the switch must be a valid Label instance.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitSwitchInsn(Label,Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:29:02.655460648Z"}
{"id":"6168cef0-2a83-46d9-bea4-d8a3b2a7d2dc","expr":"labels != null","rationale":"Labels array should be non-null to represent case labels.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitSwitchInsn(Label,Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:29:02.655460648Z"}
{"id":"68946ef2-baee-4a81-96a6-76b9a1b3b4ec","expr":"labels.length > 0","rationale":"There must be at least one label in the labels array for non-empty switch.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitSwitchInsn(Label,Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:29:02.655460648Z"}
{"id":"c590ddfb-ca0d-464a-ac0c-bc4081e03979","expr":"(! (labels.length > 0) || labels[0] != null)","rationale":"If labels are present, then the first label is not null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitSwitchInsn(Label,Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:29:02.655460648Z"}
{"id":"2763a161-5ff0-4987-849d-85e0e39f700c","expr":"dflt != null","rationale":"The default label dflt must not be null as it represents the default branch target of the switch.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitSwitchInsn(Label,Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:29:02.687985242Z"}
{"id":"67684030-f2d7-4ef7-a68b-a18e53896adf","expr":"labels != null && labels.length >= 0","rationale":"The labels array must exist and can have zero or more labels as targets for the switch cases.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitSwitchInsn(Label,Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:29:02.687985242Z"}
{"id":"c9d4754a-fe3d-416c-9b30-982c59a72b3d","expr":"labels.length == 0 || labels.length > 0","rationale":"The length property of labels should correctly represent the number of case labels.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitSwitchInsn(Label,Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:29:02.687985242Z"}
{"id":"c38f52b6-df33-4e06-b499-f6da15af2577","expr":"dflt.getCanonicalInstance() != null","rationale":"The default label's canonical instance must be non-null to set flag for jump target.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitSwitchInsn(Label,Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:29:02.687985242Z"}
{"id":"45e47493-9525-4286-b1e5-0236b4a27f41","expr":"descriptor != null","rationale":"Descriptor must be non-null to be used in symbolTable.addConstantClass.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMultiANewArrayInsn(String,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:29:03.024689776Z"}
{"id":"b8be2c7c-02a2-4ccc-8556-906a8f56efcf","expr":"numDimensions > 0","rationale":"numDimensions must be a positive int as array dimensions must be at least 1.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMultiANewArrayInsn(String,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:29:03.024689776Z"}
{"id":"e262669a-6664-4aa3-b728-b18b64702fb1","expr":"numDimensions <= descriptor.length()","rationale":"In JVM type descriptors, the number of '[' chars representing array dimensions is at most the descriptor length.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMultiANewArrayInsn(String,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:29:03.024689776Z"}
{"id":"37a782fe-07fc-4b5d-b962-c4c98bebdf1f","expr":"descriptor.startsWith(\"[\")","rationale":"MULTIANEWARRAY expects a descriptor starting with '[' indicating an array type.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMultiANewArrayInsn(String,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:29:03.024689776Z"}
{"id":"ed1c49f2-1eda-4210-a57f-f0f4b9a71a77","expr":"numDimensions <= 255","rationale":"Opcode putByte(numDimensions) implies numDimensions fits in one byte.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMultiANewArrayInsn(String,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:29:03.024689776Z"}
{"id":"03bdb9fc-f98c-4404-882d-21ecbd8a1ac2","expr":"start != null","rationale":"Labels marking the start of the try block should not be null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTryCatchBlock(Label,Label,Label,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:29:03.518970761Z"}
{"id":"e618984c-0ff5-41f4-ac20-bd85aae4eceb","expr":"end != null","rationale":"Labels marking the end of the try block should not be null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTryCatchBlock(Label,Label,Label,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:29:03.518970761Z"}
{"id":"53186f62-0137-4582-be2d-d7ca43b31ed8","expr":"handler != null","rationale":"Labels marking the handler block should not be null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTryCatchBlock(Label,Label,Label,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:29:03.518970761Z"}
{"id":"e38c55ab-e563-4485-948d-a597db31a451","expr":"(type == null) || !type.isEmpty()","rationale":"The exception type string is either null or non-empty valid class name.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTryCatchBlock(Label,Label,Label,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:29:03.518970761Z"}
