{"id":"f4fededc-7b88-4272-905a-5de1a7b9451f","expr":"varIndex <= 65535","rationale":"In JVM bytecode, local variable indices fit within an unsigned 16-bit range.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:36:59.810675136Z"}
{"id":"6bd6f52b-fa96-4bf4-a99c-09b6d3fb5909","expr":"numLocal >= 0 && numLocal <= local.length","rationale":"numLocal represents the number of local variables, and local is the array of local variable types, so numLocal should be within the bounds of local.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitFrame(int,int,Object[],int,Object[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:36:59.914861314Z"}
{"id":"f15a1e59-756d-4773-b723-314c63bbde2c","expr":"numStack >= 0 && numStack <= stack.length","rationale":"numStack represents the number of operand stack elements, and stack is the array of operand stack types, so numStack should be within the bounds of stack.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitFrame(int,int,Object[],int,Object[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:36:59.914861314Z"}
{"id":"3471cda6-37bb-4040-a47d-69996ac74756","expr":"(local == null && numLocal == 0) || (local != null && local.length >= numLocal)","rationale":"The local array must have at least numLocal elements or be null only if numLocal is zero.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitFrame(int,int,Object[],int,Object[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:36:59.914861314Z"}
