{"id":"d83b6261-1a9c-4a43-8846-01ff5449e346","expr":"!((opcode >= 0) && (opcode < 200) && (opcode != 167) && (opcode != 200))","rationale":"Opcode should either be 167, 200, or one of specific jump opcodes in expected ranges.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitJumpInsn(int,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:37:20.738349598Z"}
{"id":"9bf654d9-4c30-4f7b-a7bb-6375064ae67f","expr":"varIndex >= 0","rationale":"Local variable indices in bytecode are non-negative integers.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:37:21.456001944Z"}
{"id":"607b3313-cb86-4494-ad99-0200e7438da5","expr":"increment != 0","rationale":"Increment in an iinc instruction is typically non-zero because a zero increment wouldn't change the variable (though zero increment is technically allowed, it is less meaningful.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:37:21.456001944Z"}
{"id":"03617764-790f-4df3-ac31-9770e29887d4","expr":"increment >= -32768 && increment <= 32767","rationale":"The IINC instruction operand is a signed 16-bit immediate, so increment is within this range.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:37:21.456001944Z"}
{"id":"1ea3d0b5-8039-4f7b-a914-56916ebac357","expr":"varIndex <= 65535","rationale":"Local variable indices in JVM bytecode are generally indexed within a 16-bit range.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:37:21.456001944Z"}
{"id":"23fff3cd-2c04-477c-a1f7-82f0599f41a9","expr":"varIndex >= 0","rationale":"Variable index likely represents a local variable index, which is non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:37:22.102306656Z"}
{"id":"1ea3c09b-e241-4fd4-94be-2336fd5b1af7","expr":"increment != 0 || increment == 0","rationale":"Increment can be any integer including zero.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:37:22.102306656Z"}
{"id":"df26dec0-078a-43c8-855e-07cd633ff6b8","expr":"varIndex <= 65535","rationale":"Java bytecode variable indices fit within 16 bits, so varIndex should be in 0 to 65535.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:37:22.102306656Z"}
{"id":"75345aea-1a99-406b-b747-dfc8f00466c4","expr":"increment >= -32768 && increment <= 32767","rationale":"The increment is typically a signed 16-bit value in bytecode instructions.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:37:22.102306656Z"}
{"id":"0e7d637a-0f36-4a3e-8e63-cf5cd14a2e8d","expr":"!(varIndex < 0 && increment != 0)","rationale":"If varIndex is negative, increment must be zero, which should not practically happen; this is defensive.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:37:22.102306656Z"}
{"id":"d2f9c9e4-7e26-4b30-9bd5-95f3ee7790c4","expr":"parameterCount >= 0","rationale":"Parameter count should be non-negative because it represents a number of parameters.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitAnnotableParameterCount(int,boolean):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T11:37:22.547159329Z"}
